| History                 = This suit of armor was created by [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]], with the help of [[Ho Yinsen (Earth-616)|Ho Yinsen]], when he was captured by a terrorist cell in [[Sin-Cong|Siancong]] while overseeing the testing of some weaponry.<ref>The place and moment when Tony Stark became Iron Man has changed over the years due to Marvel's [[Glossary:Sliding Timescale|sliding timescale]]. It was originally during the [[Vietnam War]] in [[Vietnam]], but it was later changed to the [[Persian Gulf]] and later [[Afghanistan]], until it was ultimately set during the fictional [[Siancong War]]</ref> It worked as a pacemaker to keep Stark's heart beating after shrapnel from the detonation of a land mine became lodged in his chest. The armor doubled as a means for Stark to escape captivity and avenge Yinsen's death at the hands of their captors.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39 004.jpg|thumb|left]]
The suit was later upgraded into its MK II version by Stark when he returned to the [[United States of America|United States]]. The most notorious change was present in the chestplate. After realizing he would need to wear that piece of the suit at all times, Stark made it lighter and sleeker.{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 244}} During one of his heroics, Tony soon realized the dull gray appearance of the armor terrified not only his enemies but also the innocent people he was trying to protect. Stark decided to paint its shell gold, after his date [[Marianne Rodgers (Earth-616)|Marion Rodgers]] commented how Iron Man would look better with a paint job that could make him look like a knight in shining armor.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} The gold-plated version became the MK III,{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} and Iron Man soon gained the nickname of "The Golden Avenger."{{citation needed}} Tony was forced to create a partial duplicate of the suit after being kidnapped to [[Netheria|Netherworld]] without access to the parts of original armor other than the chestplate that was keeping him alive.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 41}} In order to specifically fight the [[Bruno Horgan (Earth-616)|Melter]], Stark built a version of the armor that replaced any iron with aluminum, so the armor could resist the villain's [[Melting Ray MK I|Melting Ray]]. In a previous encounter with the Melter, the armor's left arm had been easily destroyed.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 47}}

Following a disastrous battle with [[Nathan Dolly (Earth-616)|Mister Doll]] which nearly killed him, Tony realized the suit was too heavy, a disadvantage that caused the suit to consume more energy than necessary to sustain its own weight. Additionally, the chestplate appeared to need recharging more often. As soon as a [[Iron Man Armor Model 2|new lighter armor]] finished being assembled, Stark stopped using the Model 1.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} Stark briefly returned to this armor when the Model 2 was stolen by small-time criminal [[Weasel Wills (Earth-616)|Weasel Wills]], requiring Stark to use the older suit against the criminal. Despite the other armour being faster and more powerful, Stark was able to use the Model 1's superior endurance to wear Wills down until he could drain off the Model 2's power.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 65}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40 003.jpg|thumb|left]]
The MK II version of this suit of Iron Man armor was far from the only significant upgrade created by Stark. After losing [[Stark Industries (Earth-616)|Stark International]] to [[Obadiah Stane (Earth-616)|Obadiah Stane]] and subsequently joining [[Circuits Maximus (Earth-616)|Circuits Maximus]] as he recovered from alcoholism, Tony built a replica of the Model 1 as a sort of rehabilitation project.{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 188}} While built largely with spare parts and physically inferior to the [[Iron Man Armor Model 5|Model 5]] suit being worn by [[James Rhodes (Earth-616)|James Rhodes]] at the time, this version would incorporate some ideas that would later be used in the [[Iron Man Armor Model 7|Silver Centurion suit]]. The most distinct difference between this "rehab" armor and the original Model 1 was the elimination of the hip-mounted power pods, a weakness Tony himself was able to exploit against the Model 5 when Rhodey, due to headaches induced by the armor, went on a rampage.{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 192}} Tony used this suit again to aid the [[West Coast Avengers (Earth-616)|West Coast Avengers]] against [[Douglas Birely (Earth-616)|Doctor Demonicus]],{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 193}} though he was forced to ditch the armor in the Pacific Ocean.{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 194}} Demonicus recovered the suit and briefly used it himself, but his lack of experience allowed him to be defeated quickly by Tony wearing components of the incomplete Model 8 and a makeshift costume.{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 196}} One version of the armor was stolen by the mob boss [[Raymond Gonzalez (Earth-616)|Raymond Gonzalez]] and worn by his henchman [[Character Index/R#Ramirez|Ramirez]], It was destroyed in a confrontation with the [[Francis Castle (Earth-616)|Punisher]].{{r|Punisher: The Prize Vol 1 1}}

Another version, code-named "MK 0," was secretly built later on, which incorporated [[Glossary:Repulsor|repulsor weapons]], a type of weaponry not implemented in Stark's suits until the [[Iron Man Armor Model 3|Model 3]]. It was kept in [[Wong-Chu (Earth-616)|Wong-Chu]]'s abandoned base in case of emergency. When Tony Stark was on the run from [[Norman Osborn (Earth-616)|Norman Osborn]] and was slowly wiping out his brain, he traveled to Siancong in order to recover the "MK 0," which was the only armor simple enough to be used in his state.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 18}} Stark tried to get to [[Dubai]], but he was intercepted in [[Iran]] by Norman Osborn, the [[Iron Patriot]], who nearly destroyed the suit and almost killed Stark. However, Stark's allies managed to leak the coordinates of the fight to media outlets, granting the fight the media coverage necessary to force Osborn to not kill Stark in cold blood.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 19}} The "MK 0" was one of the only nine suits that were recovered after Norman Osborn's fall,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 26}} and its materials were ultimately scavenged to create the [[Rescue Armor Model 2]] for [[Virginia Potts (Earth-616)|Virginia "Pepper" Potts]].{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 29}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 1 from All-New Iron Manual Vol 1 1 002.jpg|thumb|right|Model 1 Mark III (Gold version)]]
The Model 1 was recreated and kept in exposition in the different [[Hall of Armor|Halls of Armor]] owned by Stark. During the [[Fear Itself|War of the Serpent]], when [[Stark Tower (Columbus Circle, Original)|Stark Tower]] was struck down by [[Sinthea Shmidt (Earth-616)|Skadi]], [[Noh-Varr (Earth-200080)|Protector]] tapped into Stark's mainframe and controlled an army of armor that had survived the collapse, including the Model 1, to fight against Skadi, but they were easily dealt with.{{r|Avengers Vol 4 17}} Another Model 1 armor was kept in the Hall of Armor at the [[Avengers Mansion]],{{r|Avengers Vol 4 24.1}} and one later at the rebuilt Stark Tower.{{r|A + X Vol 1 17}} When Stark temporarily moved his base of operations to [[Alcatraz Island|Stark Island]], a Model 1 was displayed there.{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 5}} The Hall of Armor in the Stark Tower remained there, and it even used one Model 1 as a security drone.{{r|Unbeatable Squirrel Girl Vol 1 2}} A different Model 1 armor was brought to [[Petoskey Stone Diner]] by numerous [[Life Model Decoy|LMDs]] in hopes of being reverse engineered.{{r|Thunderbolts Vol 3 20.NOW}}

When a [[Anthony Stark (First A.I.) (Earth-616)|digital copy of Tony Stark]] confronted the real one, who had had his morality inverted with magic, it commanded an army of Iron Man armor, including the Model 1 in both its MK II and MK III versions. Iron Man hacked into the MK III version in order to learn the location of the digital Stark's mainframe.{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 8|9}} During battle against the sorcerer dragon [[Sadurang (Earth-616)|Sadurang]], the advanced technological systems of Stark's [[Iron Man Armor Model 29|suit]] became infected by magic and it transmuted into a magical armor. Unable to control the ability to cast spells the new suit granted him, Tony opted to discard the armor and return to the Model 1. The bulky suit's focus on brute strength combined with its lack of technology advanced enough for Sadurang to infect gave him the edge in battle, and he defeated the dragon.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 13}}

Following the discovery that Tony's use of a bio-engineered new body with his mind downloaded into it to overcome a coma following the [[Civil War II|Second Civil War]] meant he was purportedly a copy of the real Tony Stark who was since then dead, Stark lost his legitimacy as a real person and was deposed of his belongings.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 19}} Having embraced his nature as an artificial being, Tony became the leader of the [[A.I. Army (Earth-616)|A.I. Army]], a liberation movement for artificial lifeforms, among them androids and robots, fighting for their rights in the light of increased oppression. Tony donned a makeshift recreation of the Model 1 Armor and started going by the name "Mark One."{{r|Iron Man 2020 Vol 2 1}}

| Properties              =
===Overview===
The armor's primary function was to act as a pacemaker which electronically stimulated Tony Stark's heart to keep it beating after the shrapnel from a land mine's detonation had entered his chest.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} This ability was achieved through the use of a defibrillator circuit and flat antenna that directly stimulated the S-A signal of Stark's vagus nerve as needed with the use of a supercutaneous high-frequency electric signal.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} This function was made obsolete once Stark had been cured of his condition.{{r|Iron Man Vol 1 19}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 1 from Marvel Fact Files Vol 1 48.jpg|thumb|left|Cutaway of the suit]]
The suit's shell is made of threads of mono-crystalline iron coated with tetrafluorethene plastic, knitted together using a 3D mechanical loom. Integrated circuits called "micro-modules" were created from sheets of silicon using an e-beam writer; this circuitry, that placed 200 transistors in a square inch with wiring and associated components, could be used both as a switch and amplifier. This allowed the creation of tiny power amplifiers that could generate the amounts of electricity needed for the DC motors that provided the suit with mobility. Each small motor generated around a horsepower of power. The use of pure iron protected with tetrafluorethene allowed a 200-inch per second speed. A gauntlet alone, for example, required a dozen motors.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} The circuits of the armor are coordinated with its user's brain waves, which allow the suit to duplicate every action of the human body. But the system is not perfect, and it requires some time to get used to it.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} It also employed a {{WP|negative feedback}} body motion sensing system.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}}

The armor's first versions were powered by a flat array of miniature batteries built into its chest plate. The batteries could be recharged by plugging the chestplate into any electrical source.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} Additional high-density storage batteries were later molded into shapes that fit almost all over the interior surface.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} The "MK 0" version of this suit, an armor hidden in Wong-Chu's abandoned base in case of emergency, was powered by a [[Arc Reactor|R.T. node]].{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 18}} An automatic self-lubrication system was built into the armor, this could be used to squirt low-pressure streams of oil.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} The suit also possessed an internal air supply.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 46}}

To help with the armor's comfortability, lamb's wool was used for interior padding. The wool was later replaced by a foamed plastic that wicked moisture away from the skin and osmotically pumped it into collection cells. There it was cooled and recirculated around the outside of the body to transport heat away from any hot spots.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} The combination of hard and soft parts allowed the bulky armor to be folded and unfolded like clothes, without losing its durability.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} However, it mandated a certain procedure in unpacking the suit so that it would fit inside [[Tony Stark's Briefcase|Tony Stark's briefcase]].{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} The armor's alloy prevented the suit from being magnetized.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 42}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 1 from Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39 001.jpg|thumb|right|Interior of the armor's chestplate]]
Jet boots were the armor's main transportation system. The boot turbines made use of ordinary air, drawn in through a loose weave of iron fabric, which was highly compressed and created a jet that enabled its user to {{Power|Self-Propelled Flight|fly}},{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}}{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} or make assisted leaps.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} The Model 1 Mark III featured the first successful sub-2-inch diameter turbine. However, the thrust-to-mass ratio was too low to allow the suit to be able to hover if its user carried something as insignificant as pocket change. The sheer size of the turbine compressor produced an ear-splitting high-frequency noise which was "about a notch higher than a mosquito and millions of times as loud," making the suit gain the nickname of "Screaming Mimi."{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} A series of small silicon levers allowed the armor to keep flying straight and level; its wearer had to use body English to accomplish steering while flying.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} The "MK 0" can make repulsor enhanced jumps.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 19}} 

Other transportation systems included jet-powered roller skates for {{Power|Superhuman Speed|fast travel}} by land at 200 mph,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 45}} a miniature jet engine and four casters that could be adhered magnetically to the armor to allow for a horizontal aerodynamic travel, like a {{WP|Luge|luger}},{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 44}} and a propeller which could be clamped into the boots for travelling on water.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 44}} When he returned to the United States, Stark modified the suit into what is known as the MK II version of the Model 1 Armor. The new version included onboard O.S. (with a translator program), lenses, and heating and cooling systems.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 18}} Most of these changes were also featured in the "MK 0" version of the suit.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 18}} A MK III added improvement in the surface, with gold plating and a metal kilt to cover groin segments. Communication systems were also improved.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}}

Because the armor's helmet was made of solid iron, it had almost no flexibility. Its wearer could not breathe hard, shout due to reduced jaw movement, or even puff his cheeks. The MK II version of the helmet added water-cooled padding, directional speakers which fed sounds to its user from wherever they impinged on the suit sensors, and a head-up display; Stark called this "Environment+Information." The neck piece was a very complex assembly. A series of flat, circular motors were stacked around the user's neck, and they were surrounded by thin metal sheeting which would follow their motion. Having several motors in each neck segment motivated helical screws that allowed for very quick movements and still be very strong.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 1 from Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1 006.jpg|thumb|left|Helmet schematics]]
Stark and Yinsen provided the armor with additional offensive and defensive capabilities to double its use as a means to escape captivity.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} Miscellaneous equipment includes miniature versions of different handy tools, including a buzz saw{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} and a drill,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} public-address speakers,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} powerful magnets,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} detachable suction cups that allowed the wearer to adhere to smooth surfaces and are strong enough to support the weight of the armor for a few moments,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} an "electronic reverse-energy beam" that could redirect rays of energy,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 43}} chemical crystals that could change the composition of substances,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 43}} image inducers,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 43}} nuclear-powered clippers,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 43}} diamond-edged digging tools,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 44}} a miniature "furnace" that generates heat waves,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 45}} a fluoroscope,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 44}} audio recorders,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 46}} radio communications (enhanced by a telescoping antenna,{{r|Iron Man: Beneath the Armor}}){{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 45}} ear plugs,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 46}} and miniature jet blowers.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 47}} Some of these items appear to be stored in the suit's accessory belt,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}}{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} while others, such as the buzz saw, appear to be incorporated into the armor's fingers.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} Using the belt's panel, the armor could access the systems of Stark Industries.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 47}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Tales of Suspense Vol 1 43 003.jpg|thumb|right]]
===Offensive Powers===
The suit enhances its user's strength to {{Power|Superhuman Strength|superhuman levels}}, allowing the user to pick up a man in the air easily,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} break through metal doors,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} destroy brick walls simply by walking into them,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} crush a cannonball with ease,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 41}} tear a wall of two floors in height with one hand,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 41}} and break the fall of a missile.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 46}} Tony Stark also stated that the suit was capable of performing such feats like ripping the bottom of a ship with ease, knocking supersonic-speed bombers with a single punch, and breaking apart space missiles. However, the veracity of that statement is dubious, as Tony was trying to intimidate [[Kala (Earth-616)|Queen Kala]] of [[Netheria|Netherworld]] to prevent her from invading the Earth.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 43}} Weaponry in the armor includes a miniature flamethrower{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} and tear gas bombs.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 44}} The armor can also redirect its electrical currency to its shell, being capable of electrocuting objects by touch.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} A circular device in the center of the chest is known as the "Monobeam," a portable proton beam{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} that served the purpose of a powerful search light,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} but it could also be adapted for a heat ray.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 45}} It only had a useful range of several yards.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} The "MK 0" version of the suit was outfitted with {{Power|Energy Projection|energy projection}} capabilities via {{Power|Repulsor Ray|repulsor weaponry}},{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 18}} and can also unleash a flamethrower from a seam on its chestplate.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 19}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Tales of Suspense Vol 1 47 002.jpg|thumb|left]]
===Defensive Powers===
The armor's shell provides a degree of {{Power|Superhuman Durability|superhuman durability}}, as it is strong enough to resist gunfire,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} the bites of animals like wild felines,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 40}} the impact of a cannonball,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 41}} heat, cold, energy, and acidic attacks.{{r|Iron Man: Beneath the Armor}} However, it was not protected against potential rusting from sea water.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 41}} The suit is also equipped with an array of miniature electromagnetic generators that allow its user to manipulate magnetic fields for a variety of effects, including jamming and disruption of electrical equipment,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39|40}} and reverse magnetism, to repel metallic objects like bullets and enemy weaponry.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 39}} An electrical force field could also be created to protect the armor from energy damage.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 46}} The "MK 0" is durable enough to take several [[Glossary:Repulsor|repulsor]] blasts, missiles, physical blows from the [[Iron Patriot Armor Model 1|Iron Patriot]] and strong enough to stop its momentum powered blows.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 19}}
{{clear}}

==Sons of Yinsen==
The Sons of Yinsen built drones that were based on the 1st model of Iron Man Armor. Which had the same appearance and capabilities, with some of the same capabilities and at least one upgrade. They had flight capability and fired repulsor bolts, and were upgraded to protect them from an electromagnetic pulse. Drones which were filled with air and constructed of steel.{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 ½}}{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 31|32}}{{r|Iron Man Annual Vol 1 2000}}

