| History                 = A new armor built by [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] after he and the other heroes returned from [[Franklin Richards (Earth-616)|Franklin Richards]]' [[Counter-Earth (Heroes Reborn)|Counter-Earth]]. Health problems linked to exposure to the power systems led to Stark abandoning this design into a new "safe" armor. [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Iron Man]] had reconfigured his armor's power systems after having health problems. This new 'safe' design was somewhat larger (too big to fit in his briefcase) due to more insulation, so a special module was designed. When needed Tony could call the module to him and have it 'tessellate' around him.{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 15}}

Iron Knight was [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Iron Man]] altered by [[Morgan Le Fay (Earth-616)|Morgan Le Fay]]'s reality distortion wave. The wave caused the time period to be altered to a medieval setting altering the [[Avengers (Earth-616)|Avengers]] clothing, speech patterns and thought processes. All of the Avengers involved believed themselves to be a part of the Queen’s elite guard known as the [[Queen's Vengeance (Earth-398)|Queen's Vengeance]]. The [[Wanda Maximoff (Earth-616)|Scarlet Witch]], with the combined willpower of all the awakened Avengers, pumped power into [[Simon Williams (Earth-616)|Wonder Man]], shifting reality back to normal, and defeated Morgan in the process.{{r|Avengers Vol 3 2|3}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 3 2 cover.jpg|thumb|left]]
While using the armor, Tony recovered [[Jocasta Pym (Earth-616)|Jocasta]]'s A.I. and downloaded it through his armor. This inadvertently caused the "Ultron Imperative" to be placed inside the armor.{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 48}} While battling [[Marco Scarlotti (Earth-616)|Whiplash]] during a thunderstorm, the armor seemed to not be functioning correctly. Whiplash's improved electric whip caused a massive discharge in combination with the storm, and Tony suffered a massive heart attack as a result. When he recovered, Jocasta informed a horrified Stark that his armor had become [[Iron Man (Sentient Armor) (Earth-616)|sentient]].{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 26|28}}

[[File:Iron Man Vol 3 26 Textless.jpg|thumb|left]]
After the A.I. died saving Tony Stark, by tearing out its own cyborg "heart", it gave the "heart" to Tony to replace his damaged one, ultimately saving his life. Despite Tony also suffering a sudden change of heart and begging the Armor to let him in so that he could save them both, the Armor refused, telling its creator, "No more -- no more, Tony. Haven't you done enough already?" The Armor died after giving Tony a final goodbye. Tony buried the Armor on the island, with a grave marker reading "Here lies Iron Man, Avenger."{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 29}}

The [[Sons of Yinsen (Earth-616)|Sons of Yinsen]] found the Armor, hoping it could resurrect [[Ho Yinsen (Earth-616)|Ho Yinsen]]. Instead, they had revived [[Ultron (Earth-616)|Ultron]]. Ultron surmised that the Armor's moments of helpfulness must have come from the personalities of Jocasta and Ultron-12, who had previously helped Tony and the Avengers against him. Jocasta uploaded herself into the armor to stop Ultron, but it triggered a self-destruct sequence. It is believed to have been destroyed along with the Sons of Yinsen.{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 45|48}}

During his status as a fugitive from [[Norman Osborn (Earth-616)|Norman Osborn]], Tony used this armor again while on the run around the world.

==Capabilities==
[[Repulsors]] had variable settings such as a wide dispersal mode that fired similar to an LMG,{{r|Iron Man: Bad Blood Vol 1 2}} the armor possesses 85 Tons strength, invulnerability, and like other armors, it maintained a unibeam, and magnetism. Pulse bolts were powerful but power drain limited their usage. In addition to standard sonics, a "sonic beam" could now be fired.{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 6}}{{r|Iron Man: Bad Blood Vol 1 2}} The armor was able to damage the [[War Machine Armor Model 3|War Machine Armor]] (modern at the time) with all power put into the palm repulsors.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 11}} The armor could also fire flamethrowers from it's back and fire a laser from its right index finger.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 12}} When transformed into the Iron Knight, [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Iron Man]] could suit-up through a single helmet, fly, and fire blasts of force through magic.{{r|Avengers Vol 3 2}}

Explosive and tear gas pellets were stored in the left gauntlet and flame-retardant foam was also stored. The armor comes equipped with a thermocouple strong enough to instantly reduce the heat from a [[Dreadnought (Robot)|Dreadnought]].{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 2}} The armor's communications with enhanced with a cellular phone and wireless modem. Sensor upgrades included radar, acoustic, thermo, seismo, MRI, helmet could create a transparent overlay, and sensor waves that can trigger an avalanche.{{r|Iron Man Vol 3 2}} A later add-on was a force bubble projector. This "hamster ball" provided protection for civilians. A chin toggle was used for convenience (drinking water) and as a backup if the cybernetic link became damaged. Also, the armor had the ability to be stored in a suitcase and fly out to envelop the user.{{r|Iron Man: Bad Blood Vol 1 1}} The armor could hack into the frequency of armaments to control them and could fire a gaussing beam that magnetizes every single metal part in an object.{{r|Iron Man: Bad Blood Vol 1 1}} The armor can opaque the eye slits in response to bright lights, see in infrared, and shut off electric magnetism.{{r|Iron Man: Bad Blood Vol 1 2}} The armor comes equipped with life-support systems and the ability function underwater without add-ons.{{r|Avengers Vol 3 9}}

The armor is durable enough to tank hits from [[Chen Lu (Earth-616)|Radioactive Man]],{{r|Iron Man: Legacy Vol 1 4}} take a direct salvo from the [[War Machine Armor Model 3|War Machine Armor]] (modern at the time),{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 11}} and take several powerful blows from [[Namor McKenzie (Earth-616)|Namor]].{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 12}} The armor is durable enough to take blows from [[Moses Magnum (Earth-616)|Magnum]] who was stated to have the seismic power to level cities and raise mountains.{{r|Avengers Vol 3 9}}

* {{Power|Telepathic Immunity}}: Stark developed counter-measures against mind control after his manipulation by [[Nathaniel Richards (Immortus) (Earth-6311)|Immortus]].{{r|Avengers Annual Vol 1 2001}}

