| History                 = After a disastrous battle with the criminal known as [[Nathan Dolly (Earth-616)|Mister Doll]], [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] came to realize that the [[Iron Man Armor Model 1]] was too cumbersome, especially in his state, which caused an excessive use of energy for the armor to simply sustain its own weight. To remedy this, Tony designed a sleeker, lightweight armor.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Tales of Suspense Vol 1 59 cover.jpg|thumb|left]]
A brief time after donning the Model 2 for the first time, Tony designed a stronger, lighter, and more comfortable helmet for it.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 54}} When Tony Stark undertook Stark Resilient, one of the models of this armor was melted to create the [[Iron Man Armor Model 37]].{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 26}}

After Tony suffered an almost-fatal mental attack by the [[Jerald (Earth-7511)|Black Lama]], he created a full back-up of his mind in case he was subjected to a similar assault in the future. Having downloaded the back-up into a version of the Mark 2 armor, he then subjected himself to a short-term mind-wipe so that he would forget about the A.I.'s creation.{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 7}} It returned when he was subjected to the moral inversion during a clash with Red Onslaught,{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 1}} but Tony was able to subvert and disable it,{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 7}} forcing the A.I. to transfer itself into [[Iron Man Armor Model 7]].{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 8}}

==Properties==
===Overview===
This suit is essentially a lighter, more flexible and more maneuverable version of Tony Stark's original Iron Man Armor. For example, the chestplate was reduced in thickness to a "wafer-thin" layer, and the helmet was redesigned in such a way it was so light, Stark claimed it can be barely felt it's being worn. The reduction in weight allowed Stark to add more protective devices. The parts of the suit subjected to more articulation, such as the legs and arms, used a malleable metallic mesh instead of solid metal plating.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} Ultra fine 3D knitting incorporated knitted motors for full motility surface.{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}}

In addition to the miniature batteries in the chestplate (with improved power-handling circuitry),{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} the armor included additional emergency battery units in the arm and leg cuffs.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} A compartment in the left gauntlet revealed a energy gauge used to keep the suit's power level in check.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 50}} The suit's batteries could be charged either by plugging the chestplate into any electrical source, or with the use of a built-in generator.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 58}} The armor carried a spare extension cord in case its user had to recharge the armor during an emergency.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 52}} In case the output of the armor needed to be increased, extra power was stored in the armor's belt pods.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 58}}

[[File:Hawkeye Vol 4 10 Many Armors of Iron Man Variant Textless.jpg|thumb|right]]
A new mechanism made suiting up the armor much faster than the Model 1, which had to be completely put on manually (a process that took one minute and a half).{{r|Iron Manual TPB Vol 1 1}} In this armor, the only parts needed to be snapped on the body were the torso, the arm-leg "adaptors" (the cuffs of the gloves and boots), the fingers and the back of the hands, and the boots' soles. Metallic meshes were pulled magnetically from the adaptors to the other sections of the armor in less than two seconds. As easily as the suit could be slipped on, it could be slipped off.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} The suit is later upgraded to be able to fly on to the user and attach separate pieces via the guantlets, the boots, the torso, the underwear, and helmet.{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 7}}

This armor is the first to implement the trademark red and yellow color schemes. Two different helmets were used with this model. The Model 2 Mark I featured a faceplate with jagged edges at the forehead, making it appear slightly horned.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} The Model 2 Mark IA sported a helmet with rivets in the forehead. This helmet was stronger and lighter, featured a built-in oxygen mask (though this feature could've been present in the previous version),{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 54}} an emergency underwater breathing apparatus that could last for roughly 15 minutes,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 58}} and oxygen filters.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 62}}

The second generation of jet boots were reduced to less than one inch thick, and allowed the armor's wearer to {{Power|Self-Propelled Flight|fly}} long distances at {{Power|Superhuman Speed|superhuman speeds}}. However, prolonged periods use would overtax them, causing the jets to exhaust until they could be recharged.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}} Similarly to the Model 1, this armor featured roller skates, which would be used mostly for short travels on land, in order to save energy that otherwise would've been used for the jet boots.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 54}} A miniature gyroscope for flight stability was located on the left boot's top.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 55}} The armor was later upgraded to handle flight in space and allow for the user to operate comfortably in the vacuum.{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 7}}

Miscellaneous equipment includes computer systems{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 62}} with radio communications{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}} (with a built-in radio antenna on the left shoulder and spare radio parts in the armor's belt pods){{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 55}} and sensors,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 61}} a generator of high-frequency waves,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 50}} powerful magnets,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}} a drill,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 51}} magnetic grapplers (to hold on to metallic surfaces),{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 54}} and a small diamond-edged blade concealed in the right hand thumb that can be activated by applying pressure in the finger's stud.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 62}} Some of these sub-miniature devices were located in the armor's flexible belt-buckle.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 55}} First aid equipment was stored within the flap of the right boot top.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 55}}

===Offensive Powers===
The {{Power|Superhuman Strength|superhuman strength}} provided by the armor allows its user to lift heavy objects with ease,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} to the point of being able to break the fall of a rocket with little effort at maximum power.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 60}} Additional power-packs located in the suit's cuffs provide the arms an extra push.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}} According to Tony Stark, this armor's gloves pack "twice the wallop" of the previous suit's.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 48}} The armor includes magnetic repulsors housed in the palm of each glove,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 55}} an electric discharge that can be fired from the armor's fingers,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 53}} and an modular electro-blaster that is magnetically clipped onto the armor's magnetic wrist holder.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 62}} The variable power chest spot-light is strong enough to dispel powerful energy rays,{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 50}} and it can still be used as a search light.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}} An add-on allows the search light to emit UV-A light.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 56}} Later versions of this armor were outfitted with [[Glossary:Repulsor|repulsor technology]], {{Power|Repulsor Ray|generating repulsor beams}} strong enough to instantly knock out the [[Jamie Carlson (Earth-616)|Teen Abomination]].{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 6}}

===Defensive Powers===
The shell of the suit grants its user a degree of {{Power|Superhuman Durability|superhuman durability}}, allowing them to resist from the gunfire of small arms{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 51}} to powerful energy blasts from [[Clinton Barton (Earth-616)|Hawkeye]]'s strongest explosive arrow tip.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 57}} The armor's insulation is even capable of protecting its user from atomic explosions at a close range.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}} The suit's miniature electromagnetic generators allows its user to create repellant magnetic force fields.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 49}}{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 54}} The suit is, however, vulnerable to rusting, thus to chemicals that accelerate this process.{{r|Tales of Suspense Vol 1 57}} The suit can also tank hits from the [[Jamie Carlson (Earth-616)|Teen Abomination]].{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 6}} The suit can effortlessly survive re-entry from space.{{r|Superior Iron Man Vol 1 8}}

