| History                 = In an attempt to stop the [[Extremis (Virus)|Extremis]]-powered terrorist [[Mallen (Earth-616)|Mallen]], [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] was fatally injured by the criminal.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 3}} Seeing no other option, Tony convinced Extremis co-developer [[Maya Hansen (Earth-616)|Maya Hansen]] to inject him a dose of Extremis to heal his injuries. Additionally, Stark had been working on an experimental Iron Man Armor that was tougher and lighter than his [[Iron Man Armor Model 25|then-current unit]]. However, he couldn't miniaturize the suit's control systems and other vital elements.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 4}} In order to overcome this obstacle, the Extremis dose was modified so that the crucial undersheath of the Iron Man suit was super compressed and stored in the hollows of Tony's bones. The under sheath became directly wired to Tony's brain, which allowed him to control the new Iron Man Armor with thought and even interface with other technologies.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 5}} During the [[Deviant Skrulls|Skrulls]] [[Secret Invasion (Event)|invasion]] on Earth, Tony's body was infected with an alien virus that shut down his Extremis enhancements and prevented him from making proper use of this armor.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 8}} Many years later, after waking up from a coma, Tony returned to using the Extremis Armor, albeit a version most likely adapted to his now-ordinary biology.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 4 600}}

| Properties       =
This armor used vectored repulsor fields to tessellate its 'memory metal' design. The armor formed over a gold under-sheath produced by Stark's own body. The under-sheath's regenerative systems could repair damage to wearer or armor. The armor could handle speeds excess of Mach 50{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 15}} and at around Mach 875.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 18}} The sheath and armor could surround the user before an explosion from multiple [[Repulsor]] enhanced human bombs could engulf the user before the heat even hits at close range.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 3}} The armor was durable enough to survive multiple [[Repulsor]] blasts from [[Ezekiel Stane (Earth-616)|Ezekiel Stane]] and even a blast of full power. It was also able to withstand multiple death blows from [[Ezekiel Stane (Earth-616)|Ezekiel Stane]] to the head before the armor gave out.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 5}} The armor could take hellfire from [[Ghost Rider (1,000,000 BC) (Earth-616)|Ghost Rider]], a blow from the [[Vnn (Earth-616)|Starbrand]], lightning from a [[Mjolnir]] wielded by [[Odin Borson (Earth-616)|Odin]], and a blast from [[Firehair (Earth-616)|Lady Phoenix]].{{r|Avengers Vol 8 31}} The armor took a punch from [[Khonshu (Earth-616)|Khonshu]] wielding the power of the [[Iron Fist]] and a blast from the [[Phoenix Force (Earth-616)|Phoenix Force]] wielded by [[Marc Spector (Earth-616)|Moon Knight]].{{r|Avengers Vol 8 37}} The armor survived has a blast from the [[Robert Reynolds (Earth-616)|Sentry]].{{r|Sentry Vol 3 4}}

Due to Extremis, Stark's mind could now directly access satellite networks, security systems, and other digital technologies. The armor could be piloted remotely, even simultaneously with several other models in the field. The armor could even form up around the user without any audio confirmation.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 7}} This was most likely achieved through the cerebral link between user and armor.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 8}} {{Power|Repulsor Ray|Repulsors}} were potent and had an additional "full form" version for multi-directional attacks.{{r|Mighty Avengers Vol 1 1}} The repulsors could fire soundwaves.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 2}} The armor could fire small bombs from its left gauntlet.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 1}}{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 3}} The armor can emit a cloud of nanosprites from its right gauntlet to shutdown an enemy combatant's lungs.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 5}} The armor comes equipped with a blade that can be used as both as an interface with outside systems and a stake.{{r|Iron Man: Director of S.H.I.E.L.D. Annual Vol 1 1}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 29 from Mighty Avengers Most Wanted Files Vol 1 1 001.jpg|thumb|left|Schematics for Model 29 Armor]]
Standard weaponry such as the uni-beam, pulse bolts, and {{Power|Sound Generation|sonics}} were intact. Explosive "micro-munitions" were launched from the gauntlets. The unibeam could reach temperatures hotter than the sun's surface (6,237K) at 54% output and even hotter at 73% (10,073K).{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 8}} The armor could fire foam from the dorsal side of its hand.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 8}} The armor could fire a laser from its index finger.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 1}} The armor had solar cells which could be charged and fired from the repulsors at maximum effect, instantly vaporizing vampires.{{r|Avengers Vol 8 14}} The armor could unleash 6 missiles from each shoulder.{{r|Avengers Vol 8 35}} The armor comes equipped with dual 2x4 missile launchers, dual chain guns, dual tasers, dual lasers, and dual ray guns, which are all attached to four limbs that protrude from the back.{{r|Avengers Vol 8 37}} This weaponry allowed Stark to fight evenly against the genocidal robot [[Nimrod (Earth-811)|Nimrod]].{{r|Civil War: Unmasked Vol 1 1}}

The armor had a degree of adaptability to support and protect the wearer. A ''neural net'' could counteract or adopt similar effects to superhuman powers.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 14}}{{r|New Avengers Vol 1 28}} Shields or "deflectors"<ref>They are called deflectors in [[Joe Casey|Casey]]'s minis. See {{cl|Iron Man: Inevitable Vol 1}} and {{cl|Iron Man: Enter the Mandarin Vol 1}}.</ref> could be raised for additional defense. The armor could maintain an active camouflage.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 15}} The armor could go fully black.{{r|Unbeatable Squirrel Girl Vol 2 37}} Additionally, the armor's parts could disguise as people before dropping the disguise to assemble around the user.{{r|Iron Man: Titanium Vol 1 1}} The armor could scan for Stark-tech using a photonic kill-code.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 3}} The armor could perform a wide range of search to identify heartbeats.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 3}} The armor could scan for biological and non-biological anomalies in the surrounding area.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 5}}

The armor's raw strength allowed it to damage [[Sadurang (Earth-616)|Sadurang]] and subsequently take a direct hit from him.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 12}} When the armor was turned magical, it was still able to fly and fight in the form of magic, it was also able to withstand the crushing weight of [[Sadurang (Earth-616)|Sadurang]] and still function afterwards.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 13}} Flight was now largely handed by small arrays throughout the suit; boots still contained turbines. The armor has reached speeds in excess of Mach 8, even mach 50 when it travelled from the Sydney Opera House to the Great Barrier Reef in under two minutes.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 15}} The suit can fly even faster when it travelled from Nei Monggol Province, China to the Sea of Japan in just a few seconds. This means the suit flew at around Mach 875.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 18}} Additionally, the jetboots could perform outside their parameters, showcased when the armor completely halted the momentum of a tube falling from space.{{r|Iron Man: Titanium Vol 1 1}} A "gravity grip" produced by the gloves and soles could be produced for climbing surfaces or for anchoring.{{r|Iron Man: Inevitable Vol 1 1}} The armor had gauntlet electromagnets that allowed it to hold onto tubes that rose to 160 miles over the Atlantic Ocean at max power for 4 minutes.{{r|Iron Man: Titanium Vol 1 1}}

'''{{Power|Precognitive Immunity|Immunity to Spider-Man's Spider Sense}}:''' After analyzing the [[Iron Spider Armor]], Tony figured out how spider-sense worked, allowing the armor to bypass It and even send false signals.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 14}} The chest piece could be used as a searchlight.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 1 17}} The suit has the ability to tap into its reserves and use that power to complete an otherwise difficult task.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 8}} The armor was able to take a punch from the [[Basil Sandhurst (Earth-616)|Controller]] who had absorbed the cerebral energy of thousands of people, although the hit was only a fraction of his power.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 8}} The armor has life support systems that allow the user to survive in the vacuum of space for an extended period of time.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 10}} The armor can withstand reentry from space with incredible ease.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 11}} The armor can have attachments and comfortably operate in space.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 2 1}}

It was also extremely difficult to operate without the aid of the Extremis drug, described by Stark as being "like trying to fly six stealth bombers at once". This problem seems to be a non-issue in the comic Avengers 2018 and onwards.{{r|Avengers Vol 8 1}} Even making several appearances in Tony Stark: Iron Man which seems to take place several years after Secret Wars and has [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] using the armor without issue.{{r|Tony Stark: Iron Man Vol 1 6}} It can lift a large submarine out of water and has stealth capabilities to infiltrate [[Nathaniel Essex (Mister Sinister) (Earth-616)|Mister Sinister]]'s heavily guarded lair unnoticed.{{r|Hunt for Wolverine: Adamantium Agenda Vol 1 3}}

