When [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] officially joined of the [[Guardians of the Galaxy (Earth-616)|Guardians of the Galaxy]], he created a new and sophisticated Space Armor in order to move better throughout the infinity of space without any complications.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 5}}
<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>
==Capabilities==
This armor is powered by numerous [[Arc Reactor|Repulsor Tech cores]], being the "Repulsor Core One" the one implanted in Tony Stark's chest.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 1}} It is equipped with Stark's newest A.I. called P.E.P.P.E.R., which can take over the suit in case of emergency.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 8}} It is also equipped with the "Stark Omniversal Multitasking Software"{{r|Avengers Vol 5 12}}, which allows its user to control other suits of armor located on Earth (such as the [[Iron Man Armor Model 42]]) from distances of hundreds of light-years.{{r|Secret Avengers Vol 2 4}} The suit also comes equipped with a thermocouple like older models and can take energy directly from the Repulsor Core in [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark's]] chest.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 1}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 45 from Iron Man Vol 4 8 002.jpg|thumb|left|P.E.P.P.E.R. taking control of the suit]]
Similar to the [[Iron Man Armor Model 42]] and the [[Modular Armor]], this armor's composition allows the user of the suit to attach/detach different kinds of modules to better suit the current situation.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 8}} The armor features regular weaponry such as repulsor rays that can also be fired in a wide-angle and start at three times stronger than normal and can scale further, making it strong enough to kill a tidal wave using 30% power.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 1}} Defensive systems include a forceshield{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 6}} strong enough to hold back a missile packed with enriched super-uranium travelling fast enough to reach the Earth and cover the armor to tank the blast at point-blank range.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 1}}. Additionally, the armor comes equipped with psionic shields.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 9}} The armor is durable enough to withstand the power of [[Blackagar Boltagon (Earth-616)|Black Bolt]].{{r|Infinity Vol 1 6}}

In order to access the modular ability, this armor can be "accompanied" by a mobile armory and be adapted to use different technologies.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 8}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 4 5 005.jpg|thumb|right|Back thrusters]]
Known modules include:

* Enhanced back thrusters.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 5}}

* Wrist-mounted explosive launcher.{{r|Iron Man Vol 4 8}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 2 008.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Saturn V Armor extension]]
The armor has two flight modes. Warp speed, which is used for interplanetary travel, and sub-warp speed, which reaches Mach 10 speed.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 1}}

The Model 45 also included an armor extension called the "Saturn V Armor" designed for Lunar landing. It granted the Model 45 six times the power storage of a regular Iron Man armor, kept in two repulsor batteries on the back, these batteries feed into redesigned boot jets that allow speeds higher than Mach 10.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 1}} The "Saturn V Armor" came equipped with shields, high-frequency repulsor pulses, a potent unibeam, the ability to eject repulsor batteries to use them as weapons, and create forceshields that can surround and protect the user and someone else from a repulsor battery filled with three hundred pounds of fuel.{{r|Iron Man: Fatal Frontier Infinite Comic Vol 1 3}}
