| History                 = When 15-year-old M.I.T. student [[Riri Williams (Earth-616)|Riri Williams]] managed to reverse engineer some of his past armor technology and posted it online, [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] saw his place under the limelight compromised. In order to remain ahead of the technological curve, Tony decided to shut himself off in his lab and make up for the time he hadn't spent working on new inventions. The end result was the Model-Prime Armor, a new suit of armor that could change shape and color based on the task at hand, essentially merging all of his armor modes into a single suit.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1 003.jpg|thumb|left|175px]]
When the armor was early in development, and it didn't possess the full version's main feature, namely a shape-shifting scaled surface, Stark was abducted to [[Earth-15513|Battlerealm]] in order to take part in the [[Taneleer Tivan (Earth-616)|Collector]]'s [[Contest of Champions Vol 1|Contest of Champions]].{{r|Contest of Champions Vol 1 3}} This prototype suffered heavy damage in a fight against an alternate-reality [[Mister Fixit|Mr. Fixit]].{{r|Contest of Champions Vol 1 1}} Seeing as Stark was no longer of use to him without a fully-functioning armor, the Collector teleported him back to Earth with no clear memory of recent events, leaving the damaged prototype behind.{{r|Contest of Champions Vol 1 3}}

The suit's final version was finished a few hours before Tony Stark's first date with [[Amara Perera (Earth-616)|Dr. Amara Perera]], for which he had to postpone testing it. Tony first suited up when he was alerted of [[Whitney Frost (Earth-616)|Madame Masque]]'s return, and had to fly to [[Latveria]] to investigate her activities.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}} During a rescue mission to save [[James Rhodes (Earth-616)|War Machine]] from the [[Southeast Asia Crime Syndicate (Earth-616)|Southeast Asia Crime Syndicate]], Tony lost one of the units he had produced of the Model-Prime Armor to the [[Tomoe (Earth-616)|Techno Golem]], a technopath who stripped Tony and War Machine of their suits to build her own.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 7}}

[[File:Victor von Doom (Earth-616) from Marvel 2-In-One Vol 1 3 003.jpg|thumb|right|As worn by Victor von Doom]]
On two different occasions, Tony had assistance from a second self-piloted unit of the Model-Prime Armor while wearing one himself, first when fighting [[Cassandra Gillespie (Earth-616)|Cassandra Gillespie]] and her Mandroids,{{r|International Iron Man Vol 1 5}} and later on when he infiltrated [[New Attilan]] in order to kidnap the [[Inhumans (Inhomo supremis)|Inhuman]] [[Ulysses Cain (Earth-616)|Ulysses Cain]].{{r|Civil War II Vol 1 2}} When the [[Civil War II|second superhuman Civil War]] came to a close, Tony switched from the Model-Prime Armor to a new [[Iron Man Armor Model 54|suit]] created specifically to fight [[Carol Danvers (Earth-616)|Captain Marvel]].{{r|Civil War II Vol 1 7}} After Tony fell into a coma during battle,{{r|Civil War II Vol 1 8}} units of the Model-Prime Armor remained in display in some of Tony Stark's labs.{{r|Infamous Iron Man Vol 1 1}}{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 4 6}} One of these models was stolen by the reformed [[Victor von Doom (Earth-616)|Victor von Doom]] and repurposed into his own version of the Iron Man Armor when he took it upon himself to carry on Iron Man's legacy.{{r|Infamous Iron Man Vol 1 1}} When Tony recovered from his injuries and resurfaced, he made use of the Model-Prime Armor for a brief time before switching to a version of the [[Iron Man Armor Model 29|Extremis Armor]] that was most likely adapted to his now-ordinary biology.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 4 599|600}}

==Properties==
[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1 002.jpg|thumb|left|100px|Suit-up]]
===Overview===
The main purpose of this suit is to serve as an all-in-one tool set. The mostly-hexagonal scales that comprise the surface of the armor can be commanded to separate and reconfigure themselves into any form and color using nanotech principles of molecular recognition.{{r|All-New, All-Different Marvel Universe Vol 1 1}} This ability makes it possible for the limbs of the suit to take the form of different tools, and even allow the entire appearance of the armor to be modified, by changing the color and mass of the suit, in order to adapt to the task at hand, including stealth operations, heavy lifting, and orbital flight. After taking shape, the scales smooth themselves out along the body's contours to give a leaner feel to the armor.<ref>{{cl|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}}, [[:File:Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1 Design Variant.jpg|Design Variant]] cover</ref>  Some of the forms the Model-Prime Armor has taken are: a [[Hulkbuster]]-like physique,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 2}} [[Stealth Armor|stealth armor]],{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 3}} a reinforced appearance inspired by {{WP|Samurai}}, and a kid-sized mode.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 4}}

Unlike other armor that were connected to the wielder's biology, this one only requires a direct link to the user's brain synapses. When not in use, the Model-Prime Armor can be collapsed into a bracelet on the wrist of the user, which can be activated and forms around the user's entire body when called upon. When the user wants to show their face, the faceplate can split apart and retract inside of the helmet entirely. Recharging the armor from scratch takes at least three hours.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 2 003.jpg|thumb|right|Shape-shifting]]
The Model-Prime Armor can reach the speed of sound right from lift-off, and additional thrusters can be formed from the suit's scales to reach higher speeds.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 3}} Flight while in stealth mode appears to leave no repulsor energy trail, so it could be powered by other means.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 3}} [[Friday Stark (Earth-616)|Friday]] is featured as the on-board A.I., which controls the suit's communication systems and scanners, among other tasks.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}} The armor can also release miniature drones for environmental scanning.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 4}} The suit's systems are so advanced they can cloak its energy signature and any frequency emanation.{{r|International Iron Man Vol 1 3}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 2 002.jpg|thumb|left|Repulsors]]
===Offensive Powers===
The Model-Prime Armor features regular [[Iron Man Armor]] weaponry, namely [[Glossary:Repulsor|repulsors]],{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}} a unibeam,{{r|Contest of Champions Vol 1 1}} and a micro-missile array.{{r|Amazing Spider-Man Vol 4 15}} The repulsors have multi-vibrational capabilities, being able to damage beings with [[Intangibility|phasing powers]].{{r|Amazing Spider-Man Vol 4 12}} When the armor was retooled by Victor von Doom, he added two more unibeams in the chest, making the suit capable of firing a tribeam at once.{{r|Infamous Iron Man Vol 1 12}} Different types of weaponry can be created on the spot thanks to the armor's primary shape-shifting function. The scales on the surface of the suit can be commanded to shape themselves into blades, guns, cannons, etc.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}} The armor can also create a "zero-point energy bubble" which drains an excessive amount of energy. This energy bubble can be used to attack enemies with a shockwave energy blast{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 4}} or as a force-field to contain them.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 5}} In addition to the commonplace increase in strength, the armor's shape-shifting features can enhance its user's strength even further by increasing in mass, giving the suit a bulky appearance similar to a [[Hulkbuster|Hulkbuster Armor]].{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 2}}

