[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 2 010.jpg|thumb|right|Self-cloaking|100px]]
===Defensive Powers===
In addition to the extra-durable shell protecting its user, the Model-Prime Armor has shown to be completely immune to different types of powerful attacks, namely sonic attacks{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}} and EMPs,{{r|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. Vol 1 6}} with such efficiency that its wearer might not even react to them.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 1}} The suit can also resist powerful blasts of energy that can destroy entire buildings,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 5}} and repeated blows from the likes of [[Carol Danvers (Earth-616)|Captain Marvel]].{{r|Civil War II Vol 1 5}} The armor also protects against intangibility, preventing objects and individuals like the [[Vision (Earth-616)|Vision]] from phasing through it.{{r|All-New, All-Different Avengers Vol 1 5}}

[[file:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Civil War II Vol 1 2 003.jpg|thumb|left|Stealth mode]]
The division of the suit's surface into individual tiles allows for fast repairing of damaged areas, as the scales simply realign themselves.{{r|Civil War II Vol 1 5}} The extent of this ability allows the armor to rapidly rebuild itself even after being broken down in its entirety.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 3}} The suit also possesses a cloaking mode that renders it invisible while its user remains in sight, providing its wearer with all of its protection and a deceivingly-defenseless appearance.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 2}}{{r|International Iron Man Vol 1 5}} The suit's multi-functionality allows it to render its entire surface black for stealth missions.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 3}} Additionally, magnetic force-fields can be used to attract objects at will.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 5}} In case the wearer's life is in extreme risk during battle, the Model-Prime Armor possesses an emergency protocol that causes the suit to burst and separate from its user while the device on their wrist flies them away to safety. The Model-Prime Armor then realigns itself and continues fighting in automatic control until its user accesses a remote interface and gets hold of the armor.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 3 3}}

| Notes                   = [[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Silver Surfer Vol 8 3 001.jpg|thumb|right|Zenn-Lavian Model 51]]
* When [[Zenn-Lavian]] forces attempted to use the reality-warping device known as the [[Illuminatrix]] to alter the Earth so its culture became a reflection of [[Zenn-La]]'s, Iron Man's armor temporarily became what it would look like if designed in Zenn-La.{{r|Silver Surfer Vol 8 3}}
* Tony once equipped the armor's unibeam with a {{WP|Sterile neutrino}} projector capable of neutralizing [[Marcus Milton (Earth-13034)|Hyperion]].{{r|Hyperion Vol 1 6}}
* When Victor von Doom made use of this armor, he used a series of dark arts spell cycles to enhance its technology.{{cite|ref=true|url=http://brianmichaelbendis.tumblr.com/post/165940095222/this-question-is-bugging-me-but-i-always-forget-to|title=BENDIS!|work=Tumblr|first=Brian|last=Bendis|date=1 October 2017|accessdate=5 May 2018}}
| Trivia                  = * Artist [[David Marquez]] on the design process for this armor: "[[Brian Michael Bendis|Brian]] and I wanted to really put our mark on the Iron Man canon and we knew that meant giving our run a distinct look, something that both honored the history of the character, but also felt like a deliberate step forward, so we worked long and hard to have that in place before we started on the story proper. We were particularly inspired the by the real world tech all around us. Today’s smartphones are capable of tasks that would have taken rooms full of mainframes and multiple single-purpose devices, [and] they do it with a sexy, streamlined aesthetic. Likewise, we wanted to slim down the armor and at the same time make into a kind of all-in-one Swiss army knife, capable of tackling any situation Tony may find himself in."{{cite|ref=true|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150919002544/http://marvel.com/news/comics/25114/armor_up_with_david_marquez_iron_man_sketchbook|title=Armor Up with David Marquez' Iron Man Sketchbook|work=Marvel.com|first=Jim|last=Beard|date=17 September 2015|accessdate=9 January 2016}}
* Marquez envisioned this armor like "a super hi-tech LEGO set." For the overall look, he took inspiration from contemporary car and aircraft concepts. In particular, the Lamborghini Aventador and fighter jets like the F-22 and YF-23. He also took notice of a trend in vehicle design of embracing hard edges.{{cite|ref=true|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150919002544/http://marvel.com/news/comics/25114/armor_up_with_david_marquez_iron_man_sketchbook|title=Armor Up with David Marquez' Iron Man Sketchbook|work=Marvel.com|first=Jim|last=Beard|date=17 September 2015|accessdate=9 January 2016}}
