| History                 = In order to embark on a journey of soul-searching, [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] stepped down from [[Stark Unlimited (Earth-616)|Stark Unlimited]], swore off advanced technology and moved to a [[Tony Stark's Brownstone|brownstone]] in the [[Lower East Side]]. He also did away with all of his [[Iron Man Armor|Iron Man suits]], resorting instead on a single vintage-style armor.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 1}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 5 1 004.jpg|thumb|left|Original design]]

During an invasion on [[Earth]] by the [[Symbiotes|symbiote]] god [[Knull (Earth-616)|Knull]], the host of the [[Venom (Symbiote) (Earth-616)|Venom symbiote]], [[Edward Brock (Earth-616)|Eddie Brock]], was fatally injured when stripped off it. In a desperate attempt to save his life, Iron Man set out to find a symbiote for Brock to bond with it. To this end, Stark infected one of Knull's [[Symbiote Dragons|symbiote dragons]] with [[Extremis (Virus)|Extremis]] to cut it off from the symbiote hive. In the process, the symbiote that Iron Man subdued infused into his armor and transmuted it.{{r|King in Black Vol 1 2}} Following Knull's defeat, Stark kept his symbiote, which he dubbed the [[Extrembiote (Earth-616)|Extrembiote]], attached to the armor it had transmuted, while he returned to a regular copy of the suit.{{r|Extreme Carnage Alpha Vol 1 1}}

[[File:King in Black Vol 1 2 Second Printing Variant Textless.jpg|thumb|right|The armor infused with the Extrembiote]]

After Tony interfered in the plans of the evil cyborg [[Michael Korvac (Earth-691)|Korvac]] to attain godhood, his neck was broken by the villain. The armor received makeshift modifications to return Stark to fighting form, since he couldn't risk giving up on pursuing Korvac. The rings of the armor's cervical column were welded together to stabilize Stark's spinal injury, and a morphine drip was added to ease the pain of the injury. Although unable to remove the chest and helmet of the suit, Tony managed to continue his chase to stop Korvac from acquiring the [[Power Cosmic]].{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 5}} The pursuit ended with both Iron Man and Korvac imbuing themselves with the Power Cosmic, and Tony's suit was transmuted in the process of becoming the "Iron God."{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 14}} In this form, the suit became an extension of Tony's short-lived omnipotence, as he was capable of materializing the suit out of thin air,{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 16}} and it disappeared when Tony gave up the Power Cosmic.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 18}} Stark returned to another regular copy of the armor afterward.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 20}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 5 14 003.jpg|thumb|left|The armor becoming an extension of the Power Cosmic]]

When the corrupt industrialist [[Kelvin Heng (Earth-616)|Feilong]] began targeting Tony as part of an elaborate plan to take over Stark Unlimited, he sabotaged the [[Arc Reactor|arc reactor]] generator of Tony's laboratory, causing his entire brownstone to explode. Tony was tinkering with the faceplate of the Model 70 when this happened, and it was heavily damaged. After settling down in [[Bronson's Cabs Depot]], Tony repaired the Model 70 with his limited resources, replacing the blemished faceplate for a new one that was also damaged.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 1}} During a subsequent confrontation with the [[Arthur Parks (Earth-616)|Living Laser]], Tony's makeshift mask was further damaged, forcing him to retrofit the Model 70's original faceplate, still charred from the brownstone's explosion, to the tweaked helmet.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 2}} Shortly afterward, Feilong succeeded his bid for Stark Unlimited. Becoming the owner of all of Stark's patents, he sent Tony a cease-and-desist to stop wearing his own armor.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 4}} Iron Man eventually relented, hollowing out the Model 70, Tony crumbled up the suit and crashed it into the Stark Unlimited HQ's hobby as an act of malicious compliance. As a result, Stark switched full-time  to his latest, clandestine armor, a stealth suit christened the [[Iron Man Armor Model Nil|Model Nil]].{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 9}}

| Properties              = 
===Overview===
This suit possesses the standard abilities of a regular Iron Man Armor, including {{Power|Self-Propelled Flight|flight}}, {{Power|Superhuman Strength|enhanced strength}}, {{Power|Superhuman Durability|increased durability}} and the ability to {{Power|Energy Projection|fire repulsor blasts}}.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 1}} It is equipped with computer systems that feature communications, environmental scanners, navigation and compass systems, medical diagnosis, biosignature tracking,{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 21}} molecular analysis,{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 22}} facial recognition software and radio jamming.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 1}} These are operated by a low-level A.I. named [[B.O.S.S. (Earth-616)|B.O.S.S.]],{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 1}} which is protected by an {{WP|Advanced Encryption Standard|AES-256}} encryption.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 20}} The armor can be operated remotely,{{r|Iron Cat Vol 1 4}} and B.O.S.S. can also maneuver the suit on its own on command.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 21}} Suit-up is achieved via a magnetic assembly process in which individual pieces of the armor fly to the user, encasing them in a matter of seconds. The suit-up can be triggered with a voice command, but it also responds automatically to emergencies.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 20}} Hand gestures can also be used to guide the armor's suit-up to a different target. If any part of the suit is open while its user is struck, it automatically snaps shut fast and seals tight.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 8}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 5 20 001.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Automatic magnetic assembly]]

The armor is outfitted with a hydrogen-based propulsion system.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 21}} It can break the sound barrier almost instantly,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 5}} and it can reach hypersonic speeds of approximately 4,700 mph (7,565 km/h),{{r|Iron Man/Hellcat Annual Vol 1 1|; [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] mentions that he can fly from [[New York City]] to [[San Francisco]] in 33 minutes, which entails covering a orthodromic distance of ~2,580 miles (~4,160 km)}} presenting a maneuverability capable of dodging rapid-fire lasers.{{r|Iron Man Annual Vol 3 1}} The Model 70 also features an autopilot.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 8}}

In terms of gadgets and secondary systems, the armor can extend autonomous connection cords, and deploy a set of robotic spiders for infiltration purposes, which can carry computer viruses.{{r|Iron Man Annual Vol 3 1}} As a measure for crowd control, the armor can dislodge a set of three discs from its left heel. In tandem, these warning beacons project a giant hologram of Iron Man with a pre-recorded message warning bystanders that he is tackling an emergency nearby.{{r|Captain America/Iron Man Vol 1 1}} The armor's heels can also deploy a set of roller blades similar to older Iron Man suits for faster ground travel.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 20}} Van der Waals adhesion circuits provide the armor with the ability to stick to such surfaces like high-speed trains.{{r|Iron Cat Vol 1 4}} The Model 70 is also equipped with a tracker connected to Tony Stark's phone.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 9}} When Tony Stark was critically injured and suffered a broken neck, he had a morphine drip temporarily installed into the suit's left bicep with three months' worth of supply.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 10}} The suit also possesses {{Power|Adaptation|adaptive capabilities}}, once being able to develop a contingency against a short-circuiting attack so that it wouldn't work a second time.{{r|All-Out Avengers Vol 1 5}}

When the suit was infused with the [[Extrembiote (Earth-616)|Extrembiote]], it gained the ability to project symbiotic tendrils that returned to the armor on their own. The armor's repulsor beams were also modified in such a way they could cleanse [[Knull (Earth-616)|Knull]]'s corruption off its victims.{{r|King in Black: Iron Man/Doom Vol 1 1}} The symbiote also allowed the armor to override Knull's influence on one of the [[Celestials]] under his control, granting its wearer full control over Knull's former victims.{{r|King in Black Vol 1 3}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Annual Vol 3 1 004.jpg|thumb|left|275px|Wide-dispersal fan beam repulsors]]

===Offensive Powers===
Like most Iron Man suits, this armor possesses both repulsor blasts and a unibeam. The suit's repulsor output is customizable, displaying the ability to change their configuration from regular blasts to forms such as a wide-dispersal fan beam,{{r|Iron Man Annual Vol 3 1}} and an "iron sniper" mode which fires shots the width of a quarter with maximum sound suppression.{{r|Avengers Vol 8 47}} The unibeam includes a setting nicknamed "the can opener," which possesses immense destructive potential, and is capable of destroying a fellow Iron Man suit, but is reserved for special occasions due to its limited charge.{{r|Iron Cat Vol 1 4}}

Other offensive weapons include micro-munitions, and palm-mounted,{{r|Iron Man Annual Vol 3 1}} dual shoulder-mounted,{{r|Avengers Unlimited Infinity Comic Vol 1 1}} and dual bicep-mounted protractible missile launchers.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 4}} The Model 70 is armed with at least three types of nonlethal rounds,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 1}} one of them being dual shoulder-mounted miniature machine guns that fire unidentified projectiles. The third nonlethal round is a pellet that fires from the right deltoid area and expands in contact into an immobilizing non-Newtonian sludge,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 4}} and it was designed specifically to disengage traditional jet propulsion.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 8}} From the index fingers of its gloves, the armor can fire either a stream of liquid nitrogen,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 1}} or a laser.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 2}} The suit can also generate a city block-sized EMP bubble that resets every electronic device inside its radius.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 4}}

The Model 70's autonomic propulsion systems can also be used offensively. For instance, the suit's user can fire off the armor's gauntlets to grasp enemies from a distance, and then have the glove circle its target and fire repulsors like a drone.{{r|Avengers Vol 8 51}} The armor can punch with a force of 20,000 newtons at a speed of 500 mph. When Stark made on-the-fly upgrades to fight [[Michael Korvac (Earth-691)|Korvac]], he doubled the suit's punch force to 40,000 newtons.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 7}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 5 23 001.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Stealth mode]]

===Defensive Powers===
Aside from the ability to deploy protective force fields,{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 2}} the Model 70 itself can shield its wearer from a wide array of hazards, including electric currents, underwater environments, fire,{{r|Iron Man Annual Vol 3 1}} magnetic fields,{{r|X-Men: The Trial of Magneto Vol 1 2}} low Earth orbit environment{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 4}} and psychic intrusion.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 9}} Its full durability was displayed when Iron Man managed to punch a hole through a sphere composed of [[Vibranium]] and [[Adamantium]], albeit breaking 17 of his bones and damaging the suit in the process.{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 2}} The suit could also withstand being crushed between the blows of two [[Stark Sentinel MK II|Stark Sentinels]] and remain fully operational despite superficial damage.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 8}}{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 9}}

For foreign toxic agents, the Model 70 possesses a configurable air filtration system,{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 22}} and counter-measures against ingested toxins.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 2}} The armor can also act as a defibrillator{{r|Iron Man Vol 5 3}} and a pacemaker.{{r|Invincible Iron Man Vol 5 2}} For aerial combat, the suit can deploy flares from its calves as a countermeasure against missiles.{{r|Iron Cat Vol 1 4}} For stealth purposes, the Model 70 can render its entire surface either white or black,{{r|Avengers Vol 8 47}} but it can also turn itself almost invisible using electrochromatophore multi-spectrum active camo.{{r|Iron Cat Vol 1 4}} The suit can also cast holographic decoys.{{r|Avengers Unlimited Infinity Comic Vol 1 6}}

