| History                 = When [[Advanced Idea Mechanics (Earth-616)|A.I.M.]] allied themselves with [[Roxxon Energy Corporation (Earth-616)|Roxxon]] in a bid to take over [[Stark Unlimited (Earth-616)|Stark Unlimited]], [[Justine Hammer (Earth-616)|Justine Hammer]] devised a plan to infect [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]]'s entire network with a magic-infused virus that compromised almost his entire Iron Man armory. Working fast with whatever components he could salvage from it, Stark jerry-rigged the Improvised Armor to continue fighting the combined forces of A.I.M. and Roxxon.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 2}}

[[File:Iron Man Armor Model 74 from Iron Man Vol 6 8 001.jpg|thumb|left|Upgraded Improvised Armor]]

After Tony averted Roxxon's acquisition of Stark Unlimited, Hammer left him with her [[Iron Monger Armor MK III|Iron Monger Armor]], which had been stripped of its [[Mysterium]] by her patron [[Belasco (Earth-616)|Belasco]],{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 3}} the component being key in stabilizing the suit's dark energy flow. Despite the [[Wanda Maximoff (Earth-616)|Scarlet Witch]]'s warnings not to don the Iron Monger,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 4}} Tony resorted to it out of desperation for an armor upgrade after [[Victor von Doom (Earth-616)|Doctor Doom]] took over the world. Hoping to stave off its corruptive effect if he only wore parts of it, Tony retrofitted portions of the suit over the Improvised Armor. The plan only worked partially, as the Iron Monger's corrpution affected Tony insidiously, clouding his judgement. After briefly doffing the Iron Monger add-ons into the [[James Buchanan Barnes (Earth-616)|Winter Soldier]]'s hijacked [[Crimson Dynamo Armor Mark VI|Crimson Dynamo Armor]], their corruptive effect became more readily apparent. Iron Man's magician ally [[Vishte Taru (Earth-616)|Vishte Taru]] then drew out the infection out of Tony, forging it and the add-ons into an armor for himself and returning the Improvised Armor to its original state.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 9}} The armor was later damaged beyond repair in battle against Visthe, and it was promptly retired.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 10}}

| Properties              = 
===Overview===
The Improvised Armor originated as a crude iteration of the Iron Man Armor with decreased functionality. Although it possessed the standard abilities of a regular Iron Man Armor, namely flight, enhanced strength, increased durability and repulsor blasts, it initially lacked portions of exterior plating and many secondary functions, like climate controls. The suit also needed multiple external generators to recharge, and included a digital gauge of energy levels installed on its left wrist.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 3}} The suit's on-board computer included comms systems,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 4}} but in lieu of a proper AI assistant, it is equipped with a chatbot called [[Iron.GPT (Earth-616)|Iron.GPT]] which is prone to {{WP|Hallucination (artificial intelligence)|hallucinating}}.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 2}}

Following his acquisition of the [[Iron Monger Armor MK III|Iron Monger Armor]], [[Anthony Stark (Earth-616)|Tony Stark]] upgraded the Improvised Armor by retrofitting a portion of the Iron Monger's components into it,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 6}} which greatly increased the armor's powers. These upgrades were later removed by [[Vishte Taru (Earth-616)|Vishte Taru]] when it became clear the Iron Monger Armor's magically corruptive taint was taking effect in Tony.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 9}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-616) from Iron Man Vol 6 2 009.jpg|left|150px]]

===Offensive Powers===
The armor greatly enhances its user's strength, allowing Tony Stark to catch and carry a minivan and even tackle the [[Justine Hammer (Earth-616)|Iron Monger]] into the air.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 3}} Repulsors were initially malfunctional due to a misrouting issue,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 2}} but were fixed since then.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 5}} They feature the conventional firepower of standard repulsors and a potent unibeam.{{r|One World Under Doom Vol 1 1}} The armor can also release an electrical discharge.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 6}}

The suit's biggest weapon is the [[Repulsword]],{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 5}} a massive protractible sword made out of retractable steel plating connected by plastic flexors, salvaged from an exploded [[Roxxon Energy Corporation (Earth-616)|Roxxon]] oil pipeline.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 2}} The [[Repulsword]] can be used to channel repulsor energy for a variety of uses, including long-distance discharges, slashing strikes,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 3}} and barrages.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 5}} The Repulsword can continually absorb energy from combatants before releasing it in controlled beams, one of which one-shot an amped [[Vishte Taru (Earth-616)|Iron Monger]] with plenty of energy to spare.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 10}}

===Defensive Powers===
Although self-admittedly Tony Stark's least protective armor,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 4}} the Improvised Armor was still capable of offering protection from a pummeling of energy blasts{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 5}} and machine gun fire with only mild discomfort.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 4}} The armor was able to withstand the full brunt of both magical and repulsor force from an amped [[Vishte Taru (Earth-616)|Iron Monger]], leaving the user unharmed but severely damaging the armor to a state of scraps.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 10}} The armor can also generate holographic shields to block rifle fire.{{r|One World Under Doom Vol 1 1}} The Repulsword can also be used as a shield,{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 3}} being capable of deflecting the [[Power Cosmic]]{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 6}} and withstanding the full brunt of both magical and repulsor force from the Iron Monger.{{r|Iron Man Vol 6 10}}

