| History                 = The suit was constructed by [[Anthony Stark (Earth-199999)|Tony Stark]] for [[James Rhodes (Earth-199999)|James "Rhodey" Rhodes]], likely following his advancement into nanotechnology as he worked toward his own eventual [[Iron Man Armor MK LXXXV (Earth-199999)|Mark 85]] armor, as the suit is shown to possess some minor nanotechnological upgrades, such as the ability to deconstruct and reconstruct the helmet around its user's head. Rhodey wore this suit during the [[Avengers (Earth-199999)|Avengers]]' time traveling attempts to steal the [[Infinity Stones]] from the past, wherein he was paired with [[Nebula (Earth-199999)|Nebula]] to claim the Power Stone, knocking out an unsuspecting [[Peter Quill (Earth-TRN734)|Star-Lord]] in the process. Once the Stones were assembled, Rhodey wore this suit as a way to protect himself from any ill effects the Stones within the Avengers' Gauntlet might have as [[Bruce Banner (Earth-199999)|Hulk]] used them. This was successful, but at the same time, a time-displaced [[Nebula (Earth-TRN734)|Nebula]] from [[Earth-TRN734|2014]] was bringing back [[Thanos (Earth-TRN734)|Thanos]] from the same year to conquer the Avengers and take the Stones for himself. With his return, the [[New Avengers Facility]] was attacked and demolished, trapping most of the Avengers within its rubble. Rhodey was trapped with [[Rocket Raccoon (Earth-199999)|Rocket Raccoon]] and Hulk and while the explosion and fall didn't kill him, it did destroy the suit that was protecting him, and he was forced to eject himself from it in order to escape.{{r|Avengers: Endgame}}

| CurrentOwner            = [[James Rhodes (Earth-199999)|James Rhodes]]
| PreviousOwners          = 

| Notes                   = * The word "canopy" works as a failsafe voice command to open the armor when the user is incapacitated.{{r|Avengers: Endgame}}
| Trivia                  = * This armor came about due to an issue that arose late into the post-production of ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]''. Originally, [[James Rhodes (Earth-199999)|War Machine]] was going to wear only one suit for the entirety of the movie (minus the prologue) which was bulky. During filming, an scene had been shot between Rhodes and [[Nebula (Earth-199999)|Nebula]], in which they shared an intimate moment of closeness. After shooting wrapped up, production realized the bulky armor would not fit as the actors were too close together. [[Phil Saunders]] was called in to design an additional slimmer suit for Rhodey to wear during the bulk of the film to solve that issue, and that armor became the War Machine Armor MK VI. The bulky suit was used only in the final battle of the film, and it became the [[War Machine Armor MK V (Earth-199999)|MK V Armor]]. The scene that caused this issue ended up being cut from the film.{{cite|ref=true|url= https://www.artstation.com/artwork/q9ynO2|title= ArtStation - Avengers: Endgame (2018) - Alternate War Machine Mk ...|work= ArtStation|first= Phil|last= Saunders|date= 15 June 2021|accessdate= 20 June 2021}}
* Phil Saunders only had one week to design this suit,{{cite|ref=true|url= https://www.artstation.com/artwork/q9ynO2|title= ArtStation - Avengers: Endgame (2018) - Alternate War Machine Mk ...|work= ArtStation|first= Phil|last= Saunders|date= 15 June 2021|accessdate= 20 June 2021}} and he had already moved to work on ''{{Star Wars|Star Wars: Rise of Skywalker|Star Wars: Rise of Skywalker}}''. He only had time to do some initial design alternatives, and Rodney Fuentebella took over for him and finished off the back view and final details of the suit.{{cite|ref=true|url= https://www.artstation.com/artwork/zALlbD|title= Avengers: Endgame (2018) - War Machine Mk VI Concept|work= Artstation|first= Phil|last= Saunders|date= 13 January 2020|accessdate= 13 January 2020}}
* During the design process for this armor, an idea was contemplated to make the slimmer ''Endgame'' War Machine suit an "undersuit" for the bulkier armor, something that could transform or bulk up to the MK V's form.{{cite|ref=true|url= https://www.artstation.com/artwork/q9ynO2|title= ArtStation - Avengers: Endgame (2018) - Alternate War Machine Mk ...|work= ArtStation|first= Phil|last= Saunders|date= 15 June 2021|accessdate= 20 June 2021}}
* Given Saunders' lack of time, one of the proposed designs for the War Machine Armor MK VI was recycled from an alternate design for the [[Iron Man Armor MK XLVI (Earth-199999)|Iron Man Armor MK XLVI]] which had "very War Machine-like forms."{{cite|ref=true|url= https://www.artstation.com/artwork/q9ynO2|title= ArtStation - Avengers: Endgame (2018) - Alternate War Machine Mk ...|work= ArtStation|first= Phil|last= Saunders|date= 15 June 2021|accessdate= 20 June 2021}}
